<http://data.silknow.org/image/37825809-3a0b-3c9e-8f1c-7459efca6381>
        a                  ecrm:E38_Image ;
        dc:identifier      "2017KD0214" ;
        schema:contentUrl  <https://silknow.org/silknow/media/vam/O121564_8.jpg> , <http://media.vam.ac.uk/media/thira/collection_images/2017KD/2017KD0214.jpg> .

<http://data.silknow.org/object/8eb1faf1-584f-3b69-aaec-18e949d843d5>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "This painted silk resembles the wallpapers made in Canton (Guangzhou) for export, suggesting that it might have come from the same workshops that produced export wallpapers. \n\nNeither wallpapers nor painted silk of this sort played a large part in Chinese interiors, while such painted pieces were often found in the furnishing of European homes. \n\nThis painted silk textile might have been used as a bedcover."@en , "Coverlet of painted silk, made in Guangzhou, China, 1760-1800."@en , "Painted silk coverlet with motifs of foliage and trees, birds, flowers and fruits. A square border with these motifs surrounds a square in the centre, where a solitary tree stands, with caged birds on one side of the branches and a basket of fruits on the other. A couple of pheasants stand at the root of the tree."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/e2b356c5-254c-3069-ad62-c08f41ce20c7> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/37825809-3a0b-3c9e-8f1c-7459efca6381> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/2eca3449-f2ef-30c1-bce2-7dec5e389069> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/2af4a6a6-5b90-36ef-88d7-3b7af1d15c4a> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/b212be3b-55a7-3336-95ab-363a8122af24> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/f55528e1-0165-337a-ac94-0f75479520f1> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/b48a5ab6-c463-332c-a6f2-858156b8db6b> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/edab4b32-b72d-3af7-9952-7bb6d9fdc6e2> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/9e1cbcde-871c-3efa-9632-f12084832db4> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/e7cec373-15e7-3f7d-8827-f71c84c4a094> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/143597a6-327c-3e56-96fe-bdd9bafa7951> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/69b3db00-6c25-320f-a240-58ed3b01a45b> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/6f5a3210-28d3-373b-8bee-4970d50b27ec> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/8b70c8e4-e245-399d-9c0e-317757d968b1> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/a4ea9b4b-410a-30d5-9e50-c55995fa6810> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/56899146-fd7f-3f70-935d-3afdd03dc9eb> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/9b66ea0d-d4ae-35db-9fb9-9418f49e93f3> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/91200320-d5a9-370f-a3f1-4f11191b708c> , <http://data.silknow.org/image/ba6395c6-b14a-32db-9f76-e581a3dd6b26> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Coverlet of painted silk, made in Guangzhou, China, 1760-1800."@en , "Painted silk coverlet with motifs of foliage and trees, birds, flowers and fruits. A square border with these motifs surrounds a square in the centre, where a solitary tree stands, with caged birds on one side of the branches and a basket of fruits on the other. A couple of pheasants stand at the root of the tree."@en , "This painted silk resembles the wallpapers made in Canton (Guangzhou) for export, suggesting that it might have come from the same workshops that produced export wallpapers. \n\nNeither wallpapers nor painted silk of this sort played a large part in Chinese interiors, while such painted pieces were often found in the furnishing of European homes. \n\nThis painted silk textile might have been used as a bedcover."@en ;
